^["done"]{
 # Local history: written incrementally, finalized at merge.
 ~#resolved(pointer_form): "How is a pointer spelled in source: @bc:<hash> (the card's spelling, which parses as a binding today), @bc#<hash> (p8's root with a fragment: the store is a declared root and the hash its anchor, so one reader serves both), or a string ~\"bc:<hash>\"? — @bc#<hash>, the p8 root with a fragment: the store is a declared root and the hash its anchor, so one reader serves roots and pointers (owner, 2026-10-13)"
 ~#resolved(fragment_store): "Where does a cited fragment's text live so a pointer resolves on any clone: the ignored .spw/gen/session (local only, as today), a tracked store such as .spw/bc/<hash>.spw holding text, card, and origin, or git blob objects (already content-addressed and confirmed through cat-file, but pruned by gc unless a ref holds them)? — a tracked .spw/bc/<hash>.spw holding text, card, and origin; git blobs were set aside because gc prunes blobs no ref holds (owner, 2026-10-13)"
 ~#resolved(hash_unity): "Do cite pointers, refactor selections, and the LSP index share one content hash function, decided with refactor-experiment-lifecycle ?[hash_basis] (the caches argue for raw bytes)? — one function over raw utf8 bytes serves cite pointers, refactor selections, and the LSP index; it resolves refactor-experiment-lifecycle ?[hash_basis] the same way (owner, 2026-10-13)"
}
